    <section class="tamu-about-body__section">
      <h2>Using our collections</h2>

      <h3>Rights Statements and Creative Commons Licenses</h3>
      <p>Texas A&amp;M University Libraries uses <a href="https://rightsstatements.org">rightsstatements.org</a>
      and Creative Commons licenses to help users understand the rights status of works in our collections.
      Each work includes a Rights Statement field with a badge representing its rights status; clicking the
      badge reveals more details. Some works also include a Rights Details field with additional information
      about the rights held in and over the resource. For questions about the rights status of an item,
      contact <a href="mailto:cushingreference@library.tamu.edu">Cushing Memorial Library.</a></p>

      <figure>
        <img src="https://rightsstatements.org/files/buttons/NKC.white.svg" title="No Known Copyright" alt="A sample rights statement" style="max-width:120px;height:auto;background-color:#800000;padding:1em">
        <figcaption>A Sample Rights Statement Badge</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h3>International Image Interoperability Framework (IIIF)</h3>
      <p>All content including media files and metadata are available as IIIF manifests, backed by a IIIF Image Server.
      This allows researchers to explore detailed, zoomable images directly on this site, and also re-use and re-mix the
      content in outside tools such as <a href="https://canopy-iiif.github.io/app/">Canopy</a> and
        <a href="https://projectmirador.org/">Mirador</a>, embed it on third-party websites, or query the data
      programmatically.</p>
      <p>The link to a collection's or work's manifest is available on every page under
      <strong>View IIIF Manifest</strong>.</p>
      <p>Learn more about IIIF and related projects on the
      <a href="https://iiif.io">IIIF website</a>.</p>

      <figure>
        <img src="/themes/custom/tamu_theme/images/view-manifest.png" title="Example View Manifest Link" alt="An example of how to view a IIIF manifest" style="max-width:300px;height:auto;background-color:#800000;padding:.25em">
        <figcaption>An example of how to view a IIIF manifest for a Work or Collection</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h3>Citing Our Collections</h3>
      <p>When citing items from our digital collections, we recommend the following format:</p>
      <blockquote class="tamu-about-body__cite">
        <p>[Item], [Collection], [Subject Area], Cushing Memorial Library &amp; Archives, Texas A&amp;M University.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>For example:</p>
      <blockquote class="tamu-about-body__cite">
        <p>Manuscript map of San Antonio to Austin, Edwin Everett Papers, Ragan Military Collection, Cushing Memorial Library &amp; Archives, Texas A&amp;M University.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>For questions about citing a specific item, contact
        <a href="https://library.tamu.edu/askus/contact-us.php">Cushing Memorial Library</a>.</p>

    </section>

